## Story Description
Create the two reference files needed by Phase 3 that don't yet exist: data/reference/internal_category_hierarchy.csv (3-level internal procurement taxonomy) and data/reference/keyword_rules.yaml (regex-based description matching rules). Also update config.yaml to add paths for these files.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Create data/reference/internal_category_hierarchy.csv with columns: l1_code, l1_name, l2_code, l2_name, l3_code, l3_name, unspsc_segment_code, unspsc_segment_name. Include minimum 60 rows covering L1 categories: IT (Telecoms, Hardware, Software, Cloud Services, IT Services), Facilities (Catering, Cleaning, Security, Building Maintenance, Utilities), Logistics (Freight, Courier, Warehousing, Fleet), Office Supplies (Stationery, Print Consumables, Furniture, Equipment), Marketing (Advertising, Events, Print, Digital), HR (Recruitment, Training, Benefits, Temp Labour), Finance (Banking, Insurance, Audit, Tax Advisory), Professional Services (Legal, Consulting, Engineering, Research), Direct Materials (Raw Materials, Packaging, Components), CAPEX (Equipment, Fit-out, IT Infrastructure).
- Create data/reference/keyword_rules.yaml as a YAML list under key 'rules'. Each rule has: pattern (Python regex, case-insensitive), l1, l2, l3 (optional), unspsc_segment_code, confidence (float). Include minimum 40 rules covering: toner/cartridge/printer→Office Supplies/Print Consumables (conf 0.82), catering/canteen/meal/lunch→Facilities/Catering (0.82), freight/shipping/courier/delivery→Logistics/Freight (0.82), mobile/handset/telecom/phone fleet→IT/Telecoms (0.80), software/licence/subscription/saas→IT/Software (0.80), legal/solicitor/barrister→Professional Services/Legal (0.80), recruit/staffing/temp labour→HR/Recruitment (0.78), cleaning/janitorial→Facilities/Cleaning (0.78), electricity/gas/water/utility→Facilities/Utilities (0.80), office supply/stationery→Office Supplies/Stationery (0.82), signage/banner/display→Marketing/Print (0.75), audit/accounting→Finance/Audit (0.80), consulting/advisory/management consulting→Professional Services/Consulting (0.78), training/workshop/learning→HR/Training (0.78), insurance→Finance/Insurance (0.82), security/guard/patrol→Facilities/Security (0.80), fuel/petrol/diesel→Logistics/Fleet (0.78), packaging/pallet/carton→Direct Materials/Packaging (0.80).
- Edit file: config.yaml — add to paths section: internal_category_hierarchy: data/reference/internal_category_hierarchy.csv and keyword_rules: data/reference/keyword_rules.yaml
- Verify: python -c "import pandas as pd, yaml; df=pd.read_csv('data/reference/internal_category_hierarchy.csv'); rules=yaml.safe_load(open('data/reference/keyword_rules.yaml')); print(len(df), 'hierarchy rows,', len(rules['rules']), 'keyword rules')" — prints ≥60 hierarchy rows and ≥40 rules

